<!--
Release-scoped upgrade data for the NEXT Darpan release (unreleased).
REBUILT 2026-10-03 from the generic seed files under runtime/component/darpan/data/, covering every
record added or modified between v1.5.1 and darpan main 268d218, then hand-ordered. Every record below
is copied VERBATIM from its seed file and was checked equivalent to it. Load with:
./gradlew loadDarpanUpgradeData

REBUILT, NOT APPENDED. The previous version of this file carried 3 of the 31 records then owed. 1.5.1's
pack is frozen at data/releases/1.5.1/upgrade-data.xml and must not be edited. This file is a DELTA
carrying only what changed after 1.5.1. An environment that has not yet loaded 1.5.1 must load
data/releases/1.5.1/upgrade-data.xml FIRST — this file restates a row that pack also restates, and
ordering the two the other way leaves the 1.5.1 values in place.

SCOPE: the darpan-seed files (AutomationSeedData, DarpanSystemSourceSeedData,
SourceSystemConnectorSeedData, SourceSystemConnectorFieldSeedData) plus ConclusionCatalogSeedData.
The catalog file is type="seed", which the docker entrypoint's by-type load never picks up, so this
file is the only way the conclusion catalog reaches a deployed instance.
DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED: the 88 darpan-tenant-config records added in the same range
(GorjanaConclusionRulesData, ShopifyNsBilledRuleSetData, TriSystemOrderRunsRuleSetData,
OrderLineUnitRuleSetData). They are gorjana's client configuration; an upgrade pack loads on every
instance, sm-darpan included. Load them per tenant, catalog first.

ORDERING, parent before child. Moqui's entity-facade loader inserts in DOCUMENT ORDER and does not
topologically sort, so a child ahead of its parent fails with a raw *_ibfk_* error that points nowhere
near this file. release_preflight.py sorts alphabetically and WILL break this if regenerated:
  1. EnumerationType DarpanConclusion, then its UNEXPLAINED enumeration
  2. AUT_STAT_NOT_RUN (its type AutomationExecStatus shipped long ago)
  3. the six DarpanSystemSource endpoint enums (their parents OMS / SHOPIFY / NETSUITE already exist)
  4. the eight SourceSystemConnector rows (remotes HOTWAX_ORDERS_API / SHOPIFY_REMOTE already exist)
  5. the twenty-five SourceSystemConnectorField pills, which FK their connector by systemEnumId

OPERATOR IMPACT: 42 records.

  - NEW ENDPOINTS, inert until configured: OMS_GQL (HotWax Orders over GraphQL, DAR-BE-064),
    OMS_ORDER_ITEMS, OMS_ORDER_LINE_UNITS, SHOPIFY_ORDER_LINE_UNITS, NETSUITE_SUITEQL — each an
    endpoint enum plus a connector row; OMS_GQL also gets its nine pills. No existing run references
    any of them.

  - OMS_RETURNS_GQL (DAR-BE-040 fix 3): OMS returns over GraphQL, beside OMS_RETURNS. The REST endpoint
    serves refunded returns only, so a returns run on OMS_RETURNS reports every pending return as missing
    in HotWax. Records match REST field for field, and the nine pills mirror OMS_RETURNS, so moving a rule
    set over is a source switch (HOTWAX_OMS_REST_RETURNS -> HOTWAX_OMS_GQL_RETURNS) with no rule change.
    The endpoint gate is absent-means-enabled, so it is available on every open OMS config at once. Needs
    the OMS GraphQL upgrade (gorjana has it since 2026-09-30); elsewhere the extract fails loudly. Slower
    than REST, throttle-bound: 258 s against 17 s for a 6-hour gorjana window (live, 2026-10-03).

  - SHOPIFY (orders) is MODIFIED in two columns, and one of them changes behaviour:
      filterParameterName  (none) -> sourceFilters
      evidenceFieldsJson   (none) -> the Shopify evidence map the run-conclusions feature reads
    From this load on, any source-filter rows (table RULE_SET_COMPARE_SOURCE_FILTER) saved against a
    Shopify-orders source START APPLYING; before it they were silently ignored. Check each environment before loading:
      SELECT f.* FROM RULE_SET_COMPARE_SOURCE_FILTER f JOIN RULE_SET_COMPARE_SOURCE s
        ON s.COMPARE_SCOPE_ID = f.COMPARE_SCOPE_ID ... WHERE s.SYSTEM_ENUM_ID = 'SHOPIFY'
    (adjust the join to the source's key columns). Six new SHOPIFY pills arrive with it: cancelledAt,
    displayFinancialStatus, displayFulfillmentStatus, hasPaymentTransaction, requiresShipping,
    sourceName.

  - SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS is restated (create-or-update by primary key, whole row) with two changes
    since 1.5.1: keepFieldsBase swaps the withdrawn returnWorkflowStatus for orderReturnStatus, and
    lookupMaxIds rises 10000 -> 50000. Its "Order return status" pill is new: after this load the
    endpoint's ONLY return-status pill. Its values are Shopify's own Order.returnStatus — IN_PROGRESS,
    INSPECTION_COMPLETE, NO_RETURN, RETURN_FAILED, RETURN_REQUESTED, RETURNED — which replaces 1.5.1's
    per-return field, whose in-progress value was spelled OPEN and so matched nothing an operator
    would type. Being order-wide it lands on REFUND rows too, so excluding IN_PROGRESS drops an
    in-progress order's refund rows as well as its return: deliberate, and a real behaviour change.

  - AUT_STAT_NOT_RUN: the terminal status a flowchart question under a failed one ends in (DAR-UI-048).
    ReconciliationRunResult.statusId FKs it, so flowchart runs fail without this row.

  - DarpanConclusion / UNEXPLAINED: the conclusion catalog root and its catch-all, needed before any
    tenant's conclusion rules can load.

COMPANION BUILDS. These records name fields and services that exist only in the matching connector
builds: darpan-hotwax 0a666b4+ (OMS_GQL, OMS_ORDER_ITEMS, OMS_ORDER_LINE_UNITS) and shopify-darpan
ddb681e+ (the new SHOPIFY pills, sourceFilters, SHOPIFY_ORDER_LINE_UNITS, orderReturnStatus). Against
an older build a pill appears but selects a field the extract does not contain, so every rule on it
matches nothing, silently. NETSUITE_SUITEQL needs the netsuite-darpan build that carries its extract.

ONE MANUAL STEP, carried over unchanged: a seed load is createOrUpdate and never deletes, so the
withdrawn $.records[*].returnWorkflowStatus pill (and, where the few-hour-old original was loaded,
$.records[*].returnStatus) stays behind. Both PKs are in
SourceSystemConnectorFieldWriteSupport.RETIRED_FIELDS, but that migration is ALREADY APPLIED wherever
1.5.0's migrations ran, and run#PendingMigrations skips applied ones. Re-run it explicitly ONCE per
environment, after this file loads:

    admin.MigrationAdminServices.run#Migration  migrationId=RETIRED_FIELDS  force=true

It is idempotent and a safe no-op where the stale rows never existed. Any exclusion rule saved against
returnWorkflowStatus keeps its stored expression and matches nothing after this load: re-add it on the
new pill with value IN_PROGRESS (the value changes too: REQUESTED,OPEN becomes IN_PROGRESS).
-->
